","includeInParentGallery":true,"positionQuality":"reviewed map placement","coordinateSource":"AuditMap reviewed Public Garden map placement","informationSourceLabel":"Boston Parks and Recreation","informationSourceUrl":"https://www.boston.gov/parks/public-garden","informationCheckedAt":"2026-08-06","imageUrl":"/assets/parks/boston-super/public-garden/04-boston-public-garden-may-2018-003-jpg.webp","imageSourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boston_Public_Garden_May_2018_003.jpg","imageAuthor":"King of Hearts","imageLicense":"CC BY-SA 4.0","imageAlt":"George Washington Statue and Arlington entrance at Public Garden"}},{"id":"f2b1d0c0-6873-4e02-8929-186c4cbc157b","slug":"ether-monument","name":"Ether Monument","feature_type":"destination","description":"The Ether Monument is on the garden's northwest side near Arlington and Beacon Streets. It is reached from the main paths and offers benches and shade, but it is not an entrance or staffed visitor facility.","latitude":42.3548286,"longitude":-71.0714514,"source_label":"Boston Parks and Recreation","source_url":"https://www.boston.gov/parks/public-garden","verified_at":"2026-08-06","details":{"category":"destination","includeInParentGallery":true,"positionQuality":"mapped feature","coordinateSource":"OpenStreetMap node 358276904","informationSourceLabel":"Boston Parks and Recreation","informationSourceUrl":"https://www.boston.gov/parks/public-garden","informationCheckedAt":"2026-08-06","imageUrl":"/assets/parks/boston-super/public-garden/01-boston-public-garden-36008p-jpg.webp","imageSourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boston_Public_Garden_(36008p).jpg","imageAuthor":"Rhododendrites","imageLicense":"CC BY-SA 4.0","imageAlt":"Ether Monument at Public Garden"}},{"id":"67bce431-2a84-481a-82e7-22405dd0e4ad","slug":"japanese-lantern","name":"Japanese Lantern","feature_type":"destination","description":"The Japanese Lantern is near the lagoon and central paths. It is a small historic landscape feature rather than a separate attraction, so pair it with the bridge, plantings, or Swan Boats.","latitude":42.3543925,"longitude":-71.0702883,"source_label":"Boston Parks and Recreation","source_url":"https://www.boston.gov/parks/public-garden","verified_at":"2026-08-06","details":{"category":"destination","includeInParentGallery":true,"positionQuality":"mapped feature","coordinateSource":"OpenStreetMap node 7693302800","informationSourceLabel":"Boston Parks and Recreation","informationSourceUrl":"https://www.boston.gov/parks/public-garden","informationCheckedAt":"2026-08-06","imageUrl":"/assets/parks/boston-super/public-garden/02-boston-public-garden-november-2016-002-jpg.webp","imageSourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boston_Public_Garden_November_2016_002.jpg","imageAuthor":"King of Hearts","imageLicense":"CC BY-SA 4.0","imageAlt":"Japanese Lantern at Public Garden"}},{"id":"de5bf2aa-2bdf-4247-a011-c8ff64be19b8","slug":"small-child-fountain","name":"Small Child Fountain","feature_type":"destination","description":"The Small Child Fountain is in the southwest garden near Arlington and Boylston Streets. It is an ornamental sculpture and fountain, not a splash pad or drinking-water feature.","latitude":42.3538894,"longitude":-71.0713337,"source_label":"Boston Parks and Recreation","source_url":"https://www.boston.gov/parks/public-garden","verified_at":"2026-08-06","details":{"category":"destination","includeInParentGallery":true,"positionQuality":"mapped feature","coordinateSource":"OpenStreetMap node 4408379859","informationSourceLabel":"Boston Parks and Recreation","informationSourceUrl":"https://www.boston.gov/parks/public-garden","informationCheckedAt":"2026-08-06","imageUrl":"/assets/parks/boston-super/public-garden/03-george-washington-statue-boston-public-garden-dsc09328-jpg.webp","imageSourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_Washington_statue%2C_Boston_Public_Garden_-_DSC09328.JPG","imageAuthor":"Daderot","imageLicense":"Public domain","imageAlt":"Small Child Fountain at Public Garden"}},{"id":"87c619b7-c961-4d5d-8f9c-b116a574496d","slug":"wendell-phillips-statue-and-boylston-entrance","name":"Wendell Phillips Statue and Boylston entrance","feature_type":"destination","description":"This statue is near the garden's southeast edge and provides a useful Boylston Street meeting point. The nearby entrance connects quickly toward the theater district and Arlington station routes.","latitude":42.352698,"longitude":-71.0684285,"source_label":"Boston Parks and Recreation","source_url":"https://www.boston.gov/parks/public-garden","verified_at":"2026-08-06","details":{"category":"destination","includeInParentGallery":true,"positionQuality":"mapped feature","coordinateSource":"OpenStreetMap node 7610246670","informationSourceLabel":"Boston Parks and Recreation","informationSourceUrl":"https://www.boston.gov/parks/public-garden","informationCheckedAt":"2026-08-06","imageUrl":"/assets/parks/boston-super/public-garden/04-boston-public-garden-may-2018-003-jpg.webp","imageSourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boston_Public_Garden_May_2018_003.jpg","imageAuthor":"King of Hearts","imageLicense":"CC BY-SA 4.0","imageAlt":"Wendell Phillips Statue and Boylston entrance at Public Garden"}}]}
